From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: OPLUS: report power_now at the
 nominal voltage

The OPLUS gauge counts charge only, and energy_now / energy_full are that
charge at the battery's nominal voltage (its design energy over its design
charge). power_now was the battery's voltage times its current. User space
(UPower) divides energy_now by power_now for the time to empty and the
remaining energy by power_now for the time to full, so the two bases
disagreed by voltage_now / nominal: on the OnePlus Pad 4 at 76 % (4.12 V
against 3.89 V nominal) the time to empty came out 6 % short of the
charge over the current, and below the nominal voltage it comes out long,
up to about 8 % near empty.

Report power_now at the nominal voltage when the battery has one, so that
energy_now / power_now = charge_now / current_now. The module parameter
oplus_power_nominal=N restores the battery-voltage power. The battery's
voltage and current stay available in voltage_now and current_now.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 0d8e883b226d..e8455a22c610 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -171,6 +171,16 @@ enum qcom_battmgr_variant {
 #define OPLUS_OTG_REDETECTS		3
 #define OPLUS_OTG_BOOST_MA		2000
 
+/*
+ * OPLUS: power_now at the battery's nominal voltage, the voltage energy_now and
+ * energy_full are reported at, so that energy_now / power_now is the time the
+ * charge lasts at the present current (N: the battery's voltage times current).
+ */
+static bool oplus_power_nominal = true;
+module_param(oplus_power_nominal, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(oplus_power_nominal,
+		 "OPLUS: report power_now at the nominal voltage of energy_now (default: Y)");
+
 #define OPLUS_CHARGER_ICL_UA		3000000
 #define OPLUS_CHARGER_FCC_UA		4000000
 #define OPLUS_PDO_SETTLE_MS		2000
@@ -1049,6 +1059,7 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_bat_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 			 * current as this driver reports it.
 			 */
 			int fw_uw = battmgr->status.power_now;
+			int uv;
 			s64 uw;
 
 			ret = qcom_battmgr_bat_sm8350_update(battmgr,
@@ -1060,9 +1071,18 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_bat_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 			if (ret < 0)
 				return ret;
 
+			/*
+			 * energy_now is the gauge's charge at the nominal
+			 * voltage: a power at the battery's voltage would make
+			 * energy_now / power_now (user space's time to empty)
+			 * short at a high voltage and long at a low one.
+			 */
+			uv = battmgr->status.voltage_now;
+			if (oplus_power_nominal && battmgr->nominal_uv)
+				uv = battmgr->nominal_uv;
+
 			/* uV * uA overflows 32 bits; result in uW */
-			uw = div_s64((s64)battmgr->status.voltage_now *
-				     qcom_battmgr_oplus_current(battmgr), 1000000);
+			uw = div_s64((s64)uv * qcom_battmgr_oplus_current(battmgr), 1000000);
 			val->intval = clamp_t(s64, uw, INT_MIN, INT_MAX);
 			dev_dbg(battmgr->dev, "power_now: firmware %d uW, V*I %d uW\n",
 				fw_uw, val->intval);
